From: Ely Office
Subject: Writer: replace and the CLI match text across tracked deletions

- With changes shown, Find & Replace searched node text with deleted
  words in it, so a phrase with a tracked deletion inside never
  matched (R23.2a). 0170 only skipped matches touching a deletion;
  hiding changes to replace reflows the document and moves a cursor
  sitting in deleted text.
- When replacing, the searched text drops shown deletions the way it
  drops fields and soft hyphens, and positions map back. A match
  never starts or ends inside a deletion; one inside a match is
  replaced with it, as with changes hidden. Regex back references
  read the same text. Find alone is unchanged.
- ElyFormatMatches, ElyInsertTable and ElyInsertImage (0154-0156)
  matched node text, deletions included; they now match the text
  without tracked deletions too.

